From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Kulp <dan@kulp.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Jun 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] FPP: disable cape_eeprom0-3 on BBB to avoid boot probe delay

FPP's U-Boot base overlay (fpp-base-overlay) used to disable cape_eeprom0-3
via phandle fixups so the kernel would not spend 3-5s probing the cape
auto-detect EEPROMs that FPP capes never populate.

Those labels only exist on BBB-family device trees (am335x-bone-common.dtsi).
PocketBeagle (PB1/K8-PB) includes am335x-osd335x-common.dtsi instead and has
no cape EEPROMs, so a U-Boot overlay that references &cape_eeprom0-3 fails to
resolve against PocketBeagle's __symbols__ and crashes U-Boot before the
kernel loads. The overlay therefore no longer references those labels.

Disable the nodes directly in the BBB base device tree instead. This keeps
the boot-delay fix for BBB while letting a single, symbol-portable overlay
boot on both BBB and PocketBeagle. PocketBeagle does not include this file,
so it is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Kulp <dan@kulp.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/ti/omap/am335x-bone-common.dtsi  | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/am335x-bone-common.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/am335x-bone-common.dtsi
index 1111111111111..2222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/am335x-bone-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/am335x-bone-common.dtsi
@@ -440,4 +440,18 @@ &tscadc {
 		ti,chan-step-opendelay = <0x98 0x98 0x98 0x98 0x98 0x98 0x98 0x98>;
 		ti,chan-step-sampledelay = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * FPP: disable the cape-detect EEPROMs. FPP capes do not populate the
+ * EEPROMs at 0x54-0x57, so leaving them enabled costs a 3-5s boot delay
+ * while the at24 driver probes and times out. Disabling them here (rather
+ * than in fpp-base-overlay) keeps the U-Boot overlay free of phandle
+ * references to labels that are absent on PocketBeagle, which lets the
+ * same overlay boot on both BBB and PocketBeagle. PocketBeagle does not
+ * include this file, so it is unaffected.
+ */
+&cape_eeprom0 { status = "disabled"; };
+&cape_eeprom1 { status = "disabled"; };
+&cape_eeprom2 { status = "disabled"; };
+&cape_eeprom3 { status = "disabled"; };
--
